# Forest terrain sketch (replaces the third-party Tileset.png, #189). One char = one pixel; `.` transparent.
# Same 320x112 sheet and tile ids as the old Tileset.png: a piece sits at `at <col> <row>` of the 20x7 sheet.
# The props at tile ids 29 to 137 (`prop-<id>`: the village sign, the bare trees, the ochre tufts) are the third-party sheet's own
# pixels, copied unchanged when the sheet was retired (#189, #236); they are not redrawn yet.
# Walk edge: blade tips on row 0, the straw line on row 1 (the cue), a straw and moss band, dark moss, a shadow line, and
# moss strands hanging over the soil. Soil and rock textures repeat every 16 px, so any arrangement of tiles is seamless.
# Variants (tile ids no map uses, for long floors): ground top 1-3, ground body 5-7, ground bottom 9-10, rock fill 12-13.
